WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.700
Today you are going to witness perhaps history&nbsp;
in the making. You see, we have some amazing new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:19.740
results with OpenAI’s ChatGPT, which is an AI&nbsp;
assistant that has now passed a US law school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:27.120
exam and is considered to be on the level&nbsp;
of a C+ student. What is perhaps even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:33.960
incredible is that it also passed coding interview&nbsp;
questions, particularly from Google and Amazon.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:40.560
That sounds like one more step towards the&nbsp;
human-level intelligence for an AI that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.060
just a few years ago, most people&nbsp;
thought will never be possible.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:52.980
Now, I have bad news and good news. The bad news&nbsp;
is that these are not results from a rigorously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.980 --> 00:01:00.000
peer reviewed paper, so we can’t pop the hood&nbsp;
and look inside to verify these claims. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.360
good news, ChatGPT also took&nbsp;
an MBA exam with a professor at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.180
Wharton business school at the University of&nbsp;
Pennsylvania, and we have a paper for that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:18.900
so we can look at the exact questions and&nbsp;
answers it has given, and an evaluation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:25.620
those answers as well. And the results are I&nbsp;
think, incredible. In short, this work is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:31.800
amazing leap forward, it can do absolutely&nbsp;
magical things, and then, as we saw earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:38.760
fall on its face on the simplest questions.&nbsp;
Now, hold on to your papers, because overall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:47.220
it seems to be a B to B- MBA student. Which&nbsp;
sounds incredible, but it gets even better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:55.500
because ChatGPT is no ordinary student. ChatGPT&nbsp;
is not just a student that can answer a few dozen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:02.760
questions a day. It is a student that can answer&nbsp;
more than 10,000 questions nearly instantly.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.640
Don’t forget, it also knows about so much&nbsp;
more than just business administration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.260
it knows about physics, art,&nbsp;
programming, literature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:19.140
and can recall and build on a larger body&nbsp;
of human knowledge than any of us can.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:26.640
Actually, let’s have a look at 4 more amazing&nbsp;
and recent examples of what it can do.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:33.780
One, it can write a little computer game where&nbsp;
we can fly around in a little virtual world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:42.840
and we can even control the camera with our mouse.&nbsp;
Yes, ChatGPT is only capable of outputting text,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:50.340
but there are ways to convert text information&nbsp;
into visual information. And one excellent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:56.880
example of that is computer code. This computer&nbsp;
code can be compiled into a computer game.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:03.300
And to get all this, we just need&nbsp;
to ask. In goes one text prompt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.800
and out comes a computer game.&nbsp;
Clearly, a very simple one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:14.760
but just imagine how incredible of a learning&nbsp;
tool this will be for a new generation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:20.580
Fellow Scholars. Some of which you will see&nbsp;
at the end of this episode. You’ll love it.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:28.680
Two, it can also become an incredible personal&nbsp;
assistant. Look, it checks our e-mail, okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:35.160
we expected that. Then, it tells us&nbsp;
how many unread emails we have. Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:53.100
we expected that too. And now…listen.&nbsp;
Whoa! It also summarizes the contents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:59.160
of these unread emails. How cool is&nbsp;
that? A true AI personal assistant.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:06.240
Three, here is a brilliant application that&nbsp;
ties multiple things together. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:12.960
if it has enough knowledge to be an okay&nbsp;
law-student and it is also an amazing assistant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:19.740
then have a look at this. A personal&nbsp;
assistant that summarizes the terms and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:26.220
conditions. We have all been asked to accept&nbsp;
a huge wall of legal text that no one reads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:32.760
and even if a poor soul is asked to read&nbsp;
it, that person has a very small chance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:38.880
actually understanding it. However, that&nbsp;
is no more. ChatGPT comes to the rescue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:44.580
and makes these readable for ordinary&nbsp;
humans in a hurry. I absolutely love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:52.140
this one. And it can summarize Youtube videos as&nbsp;
well. I wonder what it would say about this one.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:58.440
Four, we can also create more incredible&nbsp;
combinations. For instance, we can ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:05.640
ChatGPT a question, and have it answer in&nbsp;
